Think: For each path in temp_workspace/file_list.txt, compute its directory relative to the target base (/home/user/documents), transform slashes to underscores for a safe filename, and append the full path into temp_workspace/partials/partial_<relative_path>.txt (use partial_root.txt for files directly in the base). I'll run an awk command that reads the base from task_meta.txt and writes the per-subdirectory partial files.

Act: bash

```bash
awk -v base="$(sed -n '1p' temp_workspace/task_meta.txt)" '{
  line=$0;
  bl=length(base);
  if(substr(line,1,bl)==base){
    rel=substr(line,bl+1);
    if(substr(rel,1,1)=="/") rel=substr(rel,2)
  } else rel=line;
  dir=rel;
  i=match(dir,"/[^/]*$");
  if(i) dir=substr(dir,1,i-1);
  else dir="";
  gsub("/","_",dir);
  if(dir=="") fname="temp_workspace/partials/partial_root.txt";
  else fname="temp_workspace/partials/partial_"dir".txt";
  print $0 >> fname
}' temp_workspace/file_list.txt
